      "id": "hp0wc",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the conservation of linear momentum, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>v</mi><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is the initial mass, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math> is the initial velocity, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is the extra mass added and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> is the final velocity of the composition.</p><p>From equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>×</mo><mi>v</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
